{0 ache}

ache is an HTTP/1.1 client and server library for OCaml 5, forked from
{{:https://github.com/anmonteiro/httpun}httpun} and
{{:https://github.com/inhabitedtype/httpaf}httpaf}. The core does no I/O: it
parses and serializes messages and keeps the state of a connection.

{1 Packages}

{ul
{- [ache]: {!Ache}, the core. Start with {!Ache.Server_connection},
   {!Ache.Client_connection}, {!Ache.Reqd} and {!Ache.Body}.}
{- [ache-eio]:
   {{:https://ocaml.org/p/ache-eio/latest/doc/Ache_eio/index.html}[Ache_eio]},
   which runs ache on any Eio two-way flow.}
{- [ache-lwt]:
   {{:https://ocaml.org/p/ache-lwt/latest/doc/Ache_lwt/index.html}[Ache_lwt]},
   which runs ache on [Lwt_unix] sockets, or on any other socket through
   [Ache_lwt.Make]. A Lwt application must ignore [SIGPIPE].}
{- [ache-miou]:
   {{:https://ocaml.org/p/ache-miou/latest/doc/Ache_miou/index.html}[Ache_miou]},
   which runs ache on [Miou_unix] sockets. A Miou application must ignore
   [SIGPIPE].}
{- [ache-eio-tls], [ache-lwt-tls] and [ache-miou-tls]:
   {{:https://ocaml.org/p/ache-eio-tls/latest/doc/Ache_eio_tls/index.html}[Ache_eio_tls]},
   {{:https://ocaml.org/p/ache-lwt-tls/latest/doc/Ache_lwt_tls/index.html}[Ache_lwt_tls]}
   and
   {{:https://ocaml.org/p/ache-miou-tls/latest/doc/Ache_miou_tls/index.html}[Ache_miou_tls]},
   which run [ache-eio], [ache-lwt] and [ache-miou] over TLS with ocaml-tls.
   There is no OpenSSL runtime.}}

{1 What ache checks}

The server answers 400, 408, 414, 431, 501 or 505 to requests that RFC 9110
and RFC 9112 do not allow, and closes the connection.
{!Ache.Server_connection.create} lists the cases. {!Ache.Config.t} sets the
buffer sizes and [max_header_size], the largest head that ache reads (16 KiB
by default).

ache sets the framing of each response: it adds [Content-Length],
[Transfer-Encoding: chunked] and [Connection: close] where needed, and the
[respond_with_*] functions of {!Ache.Reqd} raise [Invalid_argument] for a
response that cannot be sent correctly.

The client gives [`Connection_closed] to each request that got no response,
and pipelines only behind requests with an idempotent method. See
{!Ache.Client_connection.request}.

{1 Examples}

The README and the [examples/] directory of the repository have complete
servers and clients for Eio, Lwt and Miou, and a table of the API changes from
httpun 0.2.
